1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Is your check engine light flashing...
or just staying on?

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,000
That blink is not the same warning
as a steady light.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,000
A flashing light usually means an active
misfire — dumping unburned fuel into a
red-hot catalytic converter.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Keep driving on that, and you're not
looking at a cheap fix anymore.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
If it's flashing: ease off the gas,
avoid highway speed, get it looked at today.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,000
A steady light is different — worth
checking soon, but not an emergency.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000
One clue, two different next steps.
Stop by and we'll take a look.
